  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "If \\(\\log_6 x=2.5,\\) the value of \\(x\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(90\\)",
    "B": "\\(36\\)",
    "C": "\\(36\\sqrt6\\)",
    "D": "\\(0.5\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "A logarithm tells us which exponent produces its argument. Thus \\(\\log_6 x=2.5\\) means \\(x=6^{2.5}\\). Writing \\(2.5=2+\\tfrac12\\) separates an integer power from a square root:\n\\[\nx=6^{2+1/2}=6^2\\sqrt6=36\\sqrt6.\n\\]\nThis value is positive, as required for the logarithm. The answer is \\(36\\sqrt6\\), choice C.",
